    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`, derived at read time.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` DTO schema (integer, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), placed after `customerCode`. This generates the field on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (returning `null` when no code is assigned). The algorithm matches the test's `luhn(...)` reference exactly.\n\nThe field is purely read-time derived (like `membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.), consistent with the existing OfficeFloor `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` response path, so no new pipeline step or entity column was needed.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
