        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe `checkDigit` helper follows the established pattern in `OwnerMapper` exactly: it's registered as an `@Mapping(target = ..., expression = \"java(...)\")` entry alongside the existing derived fields (`initials`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`), and implemented as a `default` method sitting among its siblings (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\nWhy this is the right unit:\n- The mapper already owns read-time derivation of DTO fields from an `Owner`, so a Luhn digit derived from `customerCode` at read time belongs here, not in a new class.\n- No duplication \u2014 the logic is self-contained and nothing comparable exists elsewhere to reuse.\n- The null-guard-returning-`null` convention mirrors how the DTO treats optional derived values, and the Javadoc matches the style/length of the neighboring helpers.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition is consistent with the sibling `customerCode`/`householdId` entries (`readOnly`, title/description, example), keeping the contract in sync.\n\nThe mapper is accumulating several derived-field helpers, but they are all cohesively \"owner \u2192 response derivations,\" which is the mapper's job; it hasn't crossed into catch-all territory."
